"platypodes" is not a widely accepted English plural for platypus.
Both "platypuses" and "platypi" are, though the latter is somewhat
objectionable since it's a back-formation that would be incorrect in
Greek (though, of course, English is not Greek).  Octopus is similar.

http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/platypus "plural platypuses
also platypi"

Fowler's and other usage guides recommend octopuses (with logic that
applies to platypus as well) and avoiding the -pi form (and notes that
use of a Greek plural -podes form is incorrect when there is already
an accepted English plural).


